<title>FRANCE: St Louis buys Ebro Agricolas stake.</title>
<headline>St Louis buys Ebro Agricolas stake.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saint Louis said in a statement on Tuesday its Generale Sucriere unit had bought a 15 percent stake in Ebro Agricolas from Banco Santander.</p>
<p>Local Spanish press reports said on Tuesday the price was 17.14 billion pesetas.</p>
<p>A Saint Louis spokesman declined to comment on the price but said that Ebro Agricolas, Spain's biggest sugar group and second-biggest food group, had a market valuation of 110 billion pesetas.  </p>
<p>Ebro Agricolas had 1996 sales of 154 billion pesetas.</p>
<p>Saint Louis said the purchase was in line with Generale Sucriere's Spanish development programme, which is to be an industrial partner to local operators, bringing in its experience in sugar production.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
